diff --git a/src/blog/tanstack-charts-1-0.md b/src/blog/tanstack-charts-1-0.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..0bc3ad26
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/blog/tanstack-charts-1-0.md
@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+---
+published: 2026-10-01
+draft: true
+authors:
+  - Tanner Linsley
+title: 'TanStack Charts 1.0'
+excerpt: 'A stable chart grammar for typed applications, with SVG, optional Canvas, and a documented compatibility contract.'
+library: charts
+---
+
+TanStack Charts 1.0 is here, and the biggest change is the promise around the
+API. You can build on the documented marks, scales, interactions, renderers,
+and framework adapters without treating every minor release as another
+migration.
+
+Patch releases fix defects, minor releases add compatible capabilities, and
+breaking changes to the supported API require a major release. Deprecated
+APIs remain supported through their current major version, with a replacement
+and migration instructions. The [compatibility contract](/charts/latest/docs/compatibility)
+spells out the boundaries, including the difference between a documented
+extension contract and an implementation detail.
+
+The grammar still starts with your data and the marks you want to draw. Compose
+lines, bars, areas, dots, maps, and polar views, then add the interactions your
+application needs. SVG is the default, Canvas and motion stay behind explicit
+imports, and you can bring compact scales or D3-compatible inputs.
+
+For 1.0, we tightened portable inferred types, framework hydration and cleanup,
+group-owned focus styling, map and polar transitions, and legend emphasis that
+doesn't disturb pinned selections. Bundle checks cover individual entry points,
+and performance comparisons use equivalent production builds and concrete
+workloads. That doesn't mean every chart costs the same, the imports and
+geometry you choose still matter.
+
+React Native remains experimental. Its package, Metro, Expo, and component
+checks don't establish physical-device or screen-reader support, see the
+[installation guide](/charts/latest/docs/installation#react-native-and-expo)
+for the current limits.
+
+Install the package and choose the capabilities you need.
+
+```sh
+pnpm add @tanstack/charts
+```
+
+If you're upgrading an existing chart, use the
+[migration guide](/charts/latest/docs/guides/migrating). If you're starting
+fresh, pick an [example](/charts/catalog/) and make it yours.
